    "chapter": "Grade 9 - Chapter 3: Cells",
    "yearEC": "2024 E.C.",
    "questionText": "Which of the following correctly compares the movement of molecules in passive and active transport?",
    "hasImage": false,
    "imagePlaceholder": "",
    "options": [
      {"id": "a", "text": "Passive transport moves molecules from low to high concentration, requiring energy; active transport moves molecules from high to low concentration without energy."},
      {"id": "b", "text": "Both processes move molecules from high to low concentration and require energy."},
      {"id": "c", "text": "Passive transport moves molecules from high to low concentration without energy; active transport moves molecules from low to high concentration using energy."},
      {"id": "d", "text": "Both processes move molecules from low to high concentration and do not require energy."}
    ],
    "correctOptionId": "c",
    "explanation": "The key difference is the energy requirement and direction of movement. Passive transport is the movement of substances down their concentration gradient (high to low) without using cellular energy. Active transport moves substances against their concentration gradient (low to high) and requires energy (ATP).",
